WEBVTT

1
00:00:30.208 --> 00:00:31.916
<b>In the previous verses,</b>

2
00:00:31.916 --> 00:00:36.833
<b>Lord Krishna shed light on action, inaction, </b>
<b>and forbidden action.</b>

3
00:00:36.833 --> 00:00:41.041
<b>In the coming verses, Krishna will clarify </b>
<b>the qualities of a person</b>

4
00:00:41.041 --> 00:00:47.291
<b>who has attained divine knowledge </b>
<b>and acts based on that knowledge.</b>

5
00:00:47.291 --> 00:00:49.916
<b>Arjuna had talked about abandoning the war,</b>

6
00:00:49.916 --> 00:00:56.416
<b>but Krishna is trying to advise him not to </b>
<b>abandon the duty of war,</b>

7
00:00:56.416 --> 00:01:01.791
<b>but rather to renounce all self-interest</b>
<b>attached to that duty.</b>

8
00:01:06.666 --> 00:01:09.083
<b>In this verse, Krishna says</b>

9
00:01:09.083 --> 00:01:12.666
<b>that the one whose every action</b>
<b>is free from self-interest,</b>

10
00:01:12.666 --> 00:01:18.666
<b>and who has burned the fruits of all his </b>
<b>actions in the fire of divine knowledge,</b>

11
00:01:18.666 --> 00:01:20.916
<b>is a true scholar.</b>

12
00:01:20.916 --> 00:01:27.125
<b>In other words, a true knower is one who </b>
<b>performs every action without any self-interest.</b>

13
00:01:27.125 --> 00:01:32.875
<b>Such a knower never fulfills his </b>
<b>duties for personal gain.</b>

14
00:01:32.875 --> 00:01:37.083
<b>He performs his duties for a higher purpose,</b>

15
00:01:37.083 --> 00:01:40.875
<b>for the welfare of humanity and for righteousness.</b>

16
00:01:40.875 --> 00:01:43.666
<b>Krishna is emphasizing</b>

17
00:01:43.666 --> 00:01:47.541
<b>that when we work without expecting any fruit,</b>

18
00:01:47.541 --> 00:01:50.916
<b>our purpose becomes pure.</b>

19
00:01:50.916 --> 00:01:56.041
<b>In such a case, we perform actions but </b>
<b>do not get bound by them. </b>

20
00:01:56.041 --> 00:02:00.958
<b>Imagine, just as gold is purified in fire,</b>

21
00:02:00.958 --> 00:02:05.291
<b>in the same way, by burning every attachment</b>
<b>related to that action</b>

22
00:02:05.291 --> 00:02:09.750
<b>in the fire of divine knowledge, </b>
<b>you also become pure.</b>

23
00:02:09.750 --> 00:02:15.916
<b>This is a form of 'inaction in action' </b>
<b>explained in the previous verse.</b>

24
00:02:15.916 --> 00:02:19.333
<b>If you remember, in the second chapter also,</b>

25
00:02:19.333 --> 00:02:24.833
<b>there was a mention of such a knower with </b>
<b>a stable intellect or steadfast wisdom.</b>

26
00:02:24.833 --> 00:02:28.333
<b>The repetition of this point is not a coincidence.</b>

27
00:02:28.333 --> 00:02:30.041
<b>Rather, it proves</b>

28
00:02:30.041 --> 00:02:38.041
<b>how important it is to perform one's actions </b>
<b>without self-interest for spiritual progress.</b>

29
00:02:42.666 --> 00:02:49.208
<b>A true scholar is the one who </b>
<b>acts without self-interest.</b>

30
00:02:49.208 --> 00:02:53.333
<b>This is the essence conveyed in this verse right?</b>

31
00:02:53.333 --> 00:03:01.458
<b>Many people claim to desire liberation and </b>
<b>understand spiritual principles,</b>

32
00:03:01.458 --> 00:03:05.166
<b>but do they actually attain freedom?</b>

33
00:03:05.166 --> 00:03:09.833
<b>True liberation is freedom from selfishness.</b>

34
00:03:09.833 --> 00:03:17.750
<b>One who recognizes their spiritual truth </b>
<b>and considers themself a soul</b>

35
00:03:17.750 --> 00:03:24.416
<b>will automatically be freed from the self-interest </b>
<b>arising from material desires.</b>

36
00:03:24.416 --> 00:03:26.041
<b>Consider this -</b>

37
00:03:26.041 --> 00:03:31.291
<b>the tendency for selfishness originates</b>
<b>from materiality itself.</b>

38
00:03:31.291 --> 00:03:37.791
<b>When you view yourself only from the </b>
<b>perspective of this body or society,</b>

39
00:03:37.791 --> 00:03:43.125
<b>then your every action will be an effort to </b>
<b>bring pleasure to this body</b>

40
00:03:43.125 --> 00:03:45.041
<b>and elevate your status in society.</b>

41
00:03:45.041 --> 00:03:48.333
<b>Every action will be hidden with </b>
<b>the desire for gain,</b>

42
00:03:48.333 --> 00:03:54.166
<b>and this is what binds a person to </b>
<b>the cycle of birth and death.</b>

43
00:03:54.166 --> 00:03:58.416
<b>And when you have known your spiritual truth,</b>

44
00:03:58.416 --> 00:04:02.333
<b>considering yourself simply a soul,</b>

45
00:04:02.333 --> 00:04:07.666
<b>then you will be able to live life free from </b>
<b>all the entanglements of selfishness.</b>

46
00:04:07.666 --> 00:04:11.791
<b>In such a state, no action will bind you,</b>

47
00:04:11.791 --> 00:04:14.708
<b>but will lead you towards liberation.</b>

48
00:04:14.708 --> 00:04:18.458
<b>Reflect on your own self, ask yourself:</b>

49
00:04:18.458 --> 00:04:21.916
<b>"Are you performing actions with</b>
<b>spiritual consciousness?</b>

50
00:04:21.916 --> 00:04:26.000
<b>Or are your activities merely </b>
<b>driven by materiality?"</b>

51
00:04:26.000 --> 00:04:28.166
<b>Learn from nature.</b>

52
00:04:28.166 --> 00:04:31.166
<b>The sun rises every day,</b>

53
00:04:31.166 --> 00:04:33.291
<b>giving light to all.</b>

54
00:04:33.291 --> 00:04:35.916
<b>The river flows,</b>

55
00:04:35.916 --> 00:04:38.625
<b>quenching everyone's thirst.</b>

56
00:04:38.625 --> 00:04:44.833
<b>The fruit-laden tree selflessly</b>
<b>gives fruit, doing its duty.</b>

57
00:04:44.833 --> 00:04:48.125
<b>You too, perform your duties.</b>

58
00:04:48.125 --> 00:04:49.708
<b>Selflessly.</b>

59
00:04:54.375 --> 00:04:57.666
<b>Consider this –</b>

60
00:04:57.666 --> 00:05:02.041
<b>why do disagreements occur in any family?</b>

61
00:05:02.041 --> 00:05:05.333
<b>Is it not because of materialism?</b>

62
00:05:05.333 --> 00:05:08.291
<b>How did someone else get more than me,</b>

63
00:05:08.291 --> 00:05:10.958
<b>how did someone else get ahead of me,</b>

64
00:05:10.958 --> 00:05:14.833
<b>how could someone speak to me like that?</b>

65
00:05:14.833 --> 00:05:16.000
<b>Now</b>

66
00:05:16.000 --> 00:05:19.791
<b>think once again –</b>

67
00:05:19.791 --> 00:05:25.291
<b>have we not handed over the </b>
<b>control of our lives to others?</b>

68
00:05:25.291 --> 00:05:33.208
<b>I had enough, but as soon as someone else </b>
<b>got more, contentment with life disappeared.</b>

69
00:05:33.208 --> 00:05:35.000
<b>I was fine until yesterday,</b>

70
00:05:35.000 --> 00:05:39.166
<b>but now that someone else is ahead, all joy is lost.</b>

71
00:05:39.166 --> 00:05:42.833
<b>Someone said something to me, </b>
<b>and I became upset.</b>

72
00:05:42.833 --> 00:05:47.958
<b>On one hand, a person says they want to be free,</b>

73
00:05:47.958 --> 00:05:50.041
<b>and then in the very next moment,</b>

74
00:05:50.041 --> 00:05:57.541
<b>they attach their emotions and </b>
<b>desires to the lives of others.</b>

75
00:05:57.541 --> 00:06:01.625
<b>What kind of freedom and independence is this?</b>

76
00:06:01.625 --> 00:06:03.416
<b>Freedom</b>

77
00:06:03.416 --> 00:06:08.375
<b>will never come from comparison or selfishness.</b>

78
00:06:08.375 --> 00:06:15.458
<b>There is only one way to it </b>
<b>– knowing your spiritual truth.</b>

79
00:06:15.458 --> 00:06:21.958
<b>Identifying not with this body, but with this soul.</b>

80
00:06:21.958 --> 00:06:24.750
<b>And as soon as this realization is understood,</b>

81
00:06:24.750 --> 00:06:28.000
<b>a change will come in behavior as well.</b>

82
00:06:28.000 --> 00:06:35.833
<b>Moving away from personal gain, the objective </b>
<b>will now become helping and benefiting others.</b>

83
00:06:35.833 --> 00:06:41.791
<b>Adopting this teaching of the Bhagavad Gita </b>
<b>not only changes personal life,</b>

84
00:06:41.791 --> 00:06:42.916
<b>but</b>

85
00:06:42.916 --> 00:06:49.250
<b> the entire family progresses together </b>
<b>towards spiritual growth.</b>

86
00:06:49.250 --> 00:06:58.625
<b>An environment is created where each </b>
<b>member is eager to help one another,</b>

87
00:06:58.625 --> 00:07:03.666
<b>where everyone respects each other,</b>

88
00:07:03.666 --> 00:07:06.083
<b>where others' progress doesn't sting,</b>

89
00:07:06.083 --> 00:07:07.708
<b>but</b>

90
00:07:07.708 --> 00:07:09.625
<b>gives joy.</b>

91
00:07:09.625 --> 00:07:11.541
<b>First,</b>

92
00:07:11.541 --> 00:07:15.625
<b>take the initiative yourself, put these </b>
<b>principles into practice,</b>

93
00:07:15.625 --> 00:07:19.750
<b>and then inspire the family as well.</b>

94
00:07:19.750 --> 00:07:26.333
<b>My only wish is that there be only </b>
<b>happiness in your family.</b>

95
00:07:30.708 --> 00:07:36.791
<b>The scholar is the one who </b>
<b>acts without self-interest.</b>

96
00:07:36.791 --> 00:07:44.791
<b>By applying this lesson from the verse to </b>
<b>your professional life, you can make it purposeful.</b>

97
00:07:44.791 --> 00:07:45.791
<b>Yes,</b>

98
00:07:45.791 --> 00:07:49.000
<b>this work is helpful in your livelihood,</b>

99
00:07:49.000 --> 00:07:49.958
<b>but</b>

100
00:07:49.958 --> 00:07:58.708
<b>if you change your perspective just</b>
<b>a little, its effect will then be truly wonderful.</b>

101
00:07:58.708 --> 00:08:00.625
<b>Think about it –</b>

102
00:08:00.625 --> 00:08:06.708
<b>the well-being of the organization and </b>
<b>colleagues is hidden in your every action.</b>

103
00:08:06.708 --> 00:08:09.500
<b>Even if it's not directly visible,</b>

104
00:08:09.500 --> 00:08:10.583
<b>but,</b>

105
00:08:10.583 --> 00:08:16.875
<b>your every task makes life easier</b>
<b>for some customer or another.</b>

106
00:08:16.875 --> 00:08:21.125
<b>Your every professional </b>
<b>action is for someone else.</b>

107
00:08:21.125 --> 00:08:25.833
<b>What is this if not service?</b>

108
00:08:25.833 --> 00:08:32.500
<b>But the most important thing in </b>
<b>service is the feeling of the mind.</b>

109
00:08:32.500 --> 00:08:37.166
<b>So try doing your every action</b>
<b>with this spirit of service now.</b>

110
00:08:37.166 --> 00:08:39.000
<b>For example,</b>

111
00:08:39.000 --> 00:08:42.625
<b>if you lead a team,</b>

112
00:08:42.625 --> 00:08:48.458
<b>make the progress of the people </b>
<b>working under you your goal.</b>

113
00:08:48.458 --> 00:08:49.750
<b>Teach them,</b>

114
00:08:49.750 --> 00:08:53.833
<b>contribute to increasing their efficiency.</b>

115
00:08:53.833 --> 00:08:58.833
<b>This will not only improve the work, </b>
<b>but your life will also become easier,</b>

116
00:08:58.833 --> 00:09:06.666
<b>but most importantly, a positive </b>
<b>environment will be created.</b>

117
00:09:06.666 --> 00:09:11.166
<b>This perspective also keeps you motivated </b>
<b>by saving you from frustration.</b>

118
00:09:11.166 --> 00:09:15.958
<b>Because if you are doing every task with </b>
<b>the spirit of service,</b>

119
00:09:15.958 --> 00:09:21.250
<b>then self-satisfaction will no longer depend</b>
<b>on any promotion.</b>

120
00:09:21.250 --> 00:09:28.541
<b>If promoted, there is joy, and if not, </b>
<b>there is still a smile of contentment on the face.</b>

121
00:09:28.541 --> 00:09:31.625
<b>This is also a kind of liberation, isn't it?</b>

122
00:09:31.625 --> 00:09:37.708
<b>A freedom where you are </b>
<b>happy in every situation.</b>

123
00:09:37.708 --> 00:09:40.500
<b>This is the magic of the spirit of service.</b>

124
00:09:40.500 --> 00:09:42.166
<b>Reflect on it.</b>

